\nL54: \nL55: Full Calibration\nL56: \nL57: Standard  | Drops\nL58: --- | ---\nL59: 0 NTU  | 0\nL60: 10 NTU  | 10\nL61: 20 NTU  | 20\nL62: 30 NTU  | 30\nL63: 40 NTU  | 40\nL64: \nL65: Minimal Calibration\nL66: \nL67: Standard  | Drops\nL68: --- | ---\nL69: 0 NTU  | 0\nL70: 10 NTU  | 10\nL71: 40 NTU  | 40\nL72: \nL73: You do not need to add any reagent for this test. Shake the standard solutions dropper bottle thoroughly.\nL74:   * Take the 0 standard and fill it into the glass cuvette provided. Place the glass cuvette inside the blue cuvette.\nL75:   * Place the cuvette under the light box and turn it on.\nL76:   * Place the phone over the stand.\nL77:   * Go to `Settings` > `Colorimetric Test` > `Calibrate` and choose `Turbidity`.\nL78:   * Select the calibration point, 0.00 NTU in this case.\nL79:   * Click on `Start Camera`.\nL80:   * Position the cuvette so that the middle, most uniformly lit portion is within the circle.\nL81:   * Select `Analyze`.\nL82:   * You should have your first calibration point. Repeat similarly with the other calibration points.\nL83: ## Test\nL84: \nL85: This test does not require a reagent.\nL86:   * Collect 20 ml of sample water and place in glass cuvette and in turn inside the blue cuvette.\nL87:   * Place the cuvette under the light box and turn it on.\nL88:   * Place the phone over the stand.\nL89:   * From the home screen choose `Colorimetric Test` > `Water` > `Turbidity`.\nL90:   * Choose `No Dilution` if this is the first test, you might have to dilute the sample and retry later if you get an error.\nL91:   * Click on `Start Camera`.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn3view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view2\",\"pattern\":\"four\"}); Total lines: 1\nNo matching text found for \"four\""
